1
00:00:02,990 --> 00:00:07,430
I'm so glad you're okay, Kasumi.

2
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,080
If it were me, I'd be by your side more...

3
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,440
Much more than Reo.

4
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:26,280
Am I so bad?

5
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:39,450
I…

6
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,820
thought you were my friend!

7
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:51,350
Don't decide we're friends on your own.

8
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,030
What's going on?

9
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,210
Reo!

10
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:09,210
Don't come near my girlfriend again.

11
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:16,640
Let's go.

12
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:34,870
<i>[Ai-Chan's Secret | Episode 7]</i>

13
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,600
I see.

14
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,040
So, Takumi helped you?

15
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:54,270
No other guy will see that look on your face.

16
00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:02,380
I'm sorry about yesterday.

17
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:04,680
<i>- Don't "happen to" let your guard down!
- I didn't!</i>

18
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:08,750
<i>That kindness of yours is exactly what leads other men on!</i>

19
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:13,430
I'm sorry, too.

20
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:19,700
I should have told you he confessed to me.

21
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:34,740
Takumi found out…

22
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:37,140
that I'm Mai.

23
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:40,700
I knew it.

24
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:44,100
I think he'll keep it quiet.

25
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,670
That's what he told me.

26
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,540
Were you angry?

27
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:57,600
I might have been jealous of him.

28
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:04,380
I only see Takumi as a friend.

29
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,260
That's only natural.

30
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:19,660
All right.

31
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,470
- Shall we turn over a new leaf?
- Pardon?

32
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,240
- Let's go.
- Where?

33
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,550
It's a secret.

34
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:28,650
What does that mean?

35
00:03:28,650 --> 00:03:32,300
- It's so good! Want some, Reo?
- Sure.

36
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,040
- It is good!
- Yeah!

37
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,200
- Come on! That's too much!
- So yummy.

38
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,760
That's enough. There won't be some left for me!

39
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,590
- Yummy!
- No fair!

40
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:48,630
Give it back!

41
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:56,230
- It's cold, huh?
- Yeah.

42
00:03:57,590 --> 00:03:59,800
I'm glad I brought my coat.

43
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:02,840
Thank you.

44
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,920
♫ <i>You are so free</i> ♫

45
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,220
Should we head home?

46
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:15,070
No. I don't want to go home yet.

47
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:19,100
- But it's...
- I mean...

48
00:04:19,770 --> 00:04:22,690
It's finally just the two of us.

49
00:04:26,910 --> 00:04:28,590
Then...

50
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:31,660
want to come to my place?

51
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:38,250
My mom works the night shift, so no one's home.

52
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:47,910
♫ <i>Just wanna, wanna, wanna, wanna go and take it</i> ♫

53
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:57,320
Wow! You've got good style, Reo!

54
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,700
Oh! This manga is the best!

55
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,740
- Want to borrow it?
- For real?

56
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:07,020
- Yeah.
- Yay!

57
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:14,480
But...

58
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:21,830
Do you understand the implications of coming to a guy's room?

59
00:05:59,890 --> 00:06:01,460
Aiko...

60
00:06:12,170 --> 00:06:15,840
<i>Sex appeal is key. That bra will do nothing for him.</i>

61
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,650
I can't.

62
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,770
I'm sorry.

63
00:06:24,130 --> 00:06:25,720
I can't.

64
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,690
Why?

65
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,680
Well...

66
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:40,530
It's just...

67
00:06:46,090 --> 00:06:47,690
I'm sorry.

68
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,920
I got too impatient.

69
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,700
No, it's not that.

70
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:58,370
I'll just walk you home.

71
00:07:08,110 --> 00:07:09,820
Okay.

72
00:07:19,750 --> 00:07:23,460
<i>This bra is terrible!</i>

73
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,010
Oh? A stalker?

74
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:41,820
No.

75
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:44,010
I just walked her home.

76
00:07:44,010 --> 00:07:48,560
So? Did you make my little sis a woman?

77
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,040
That's direct...

78
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,840
Well, I am her brother.

79
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:58,940
I think I might've rushed things.

80
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:03,680
I thought I'd feel less nervous if I made her mine quickly.

81
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:08,730
But Ai is really important to me.

82
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:13,270
I want to value her feelings more than anything.

83
00:08:15,450 --> 00:08:19,160
Oh, to be young! Youth is the best, huh?

84
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:21,580
Ritsuki, you reek of booze!

85
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:23,890
Let me tell you something.

86
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:28,310
<i>[Kafuu High School]</i>

87
00:08:28,310 --> 00:08:31,270
That's it? Even though you went to his house?

88
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:35,490
But the "thing" I was wearing was second-rate.

89
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:40,700
When you go to a guy's place when you're dating

90
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:43,860
- the guy sort of expects "you-know-what."
- Huh?

91
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:45,830
So that's how it is.

92
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:48,420
I don't think you have to rush it,

93
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:52,950
but as his girlfriend, you have to give it some thought.

94
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:56,300
Reo's a guy, after all. It's kind of sad.

95
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:58,790
I see.

96
00:08:58,790 --> 00:09:01,620
That's true, huh?

97
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:05,380
Let's go pick out some underwear together!

98
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:08,680
Huh? N-No! It's too much trouble.

99
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,910
- Let's go! Let's go!
- No! No!

100
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:12,550
- Let's go.
- Why?

101
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:15,410
- What do you want?
- Nothing!

102
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:28,980
I heard you helped out Aiko before.

103
00:09:30,010 --> 00:09:31,850
What's this?

104
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:34,560
I hoped she'd keep it a secret a little bit longer.

105
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:37,190
Keep your paws off my Aiko.

106
00:09:37,190 --> 00:09:41,160
Big words for someone who can't speak on her behalf.

107
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:56,420
She called you her friend, didn't she?

108
00:09:56,420 --> 00:10:00,390
Love that begins from friendship isn't so bad.

109
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:03,290
How nonchalant.

110
00:10:04,430 --> 00:10:06,650
I'm very serious.

111
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:09,240
So what?

112
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,410
We'll stop there for today!

113
00:10:21,410 --> 00:10:25,550
Tomorrow, I was thinking of having the girls go first.

114
00:10:25,550 --> 00:10:27,790
- Oh? Does Ms. Oyama know?
- Yes, she does.

115
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:31,280
That's fine, then. Got it.

116
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:34,040
<i>Don't decide we're friends on your own.</i>

117
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,640
- I'll leave it to you.
- Right. Thank you.

118
00:10:43,790 --> 00:10:46,060
Don't put your guard up so high.

119
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:48,020
We're friends, right?

120
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:52,170
Takumi...

121
00:10:52,170 --> 00:10:56,550
I want to be someone you can always depend on.

122
00:10:56,550 --> 00:11:00,340
As friends, of course. Right?

123
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,730
Right.

124
00:11:06,710 --> 00:11:08,030
Stop!

125
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:10,250
What is this?

126
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:13,080
- Don't interrupt.
- Huh?

127
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:16,050
Let the flower of love bloom in others, like it's bloomed for you.

128
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:17,670
What are you talking about? That's ridiculous.

129
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:20,560
- Wait!
- Aren't those two surprisingly good together?

130
00:11:20,570 --> 00:11:23,200
Please cooperate so things go well with them!

131
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:25,250
- Why me?!
- Come on!

132
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:28,400
Let's go. Come on, let's go.

133
00:11:31,230 --> 00:11:33,860
<i>[Are you coming to Spica today?]</i>

134
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,370
<i>[Sorry, I can't today.]</i>

135
00:11:49,820 --> 00:11:51,690
- Where's Reo?
- I don't know.

136
00:11:51,690 --> 00:11:54,040
But you're together all the time.

137
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:55,440
Wait! Reo!

138
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:58,030
He's got a date again?

139
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:02,530
- Then why don't we go on a date, too? Huh?!
- No way.

140
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:07,640
I'll take that out.

141
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:09,060
- Welcome!
- Welcome!

142
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:12,920
- Excuse me.
- Yeah?

143
00:12:12,930 --> 00:12:15,400
Oh? You're...

144
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,390
You're Aiko's...

145
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,630
Here you go.

146
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:25,030
Boss said you can take a break.

147
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:27,360
I'm okay.

148
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:31,020
When I'm working, I don't have to think about anything else.

149
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:35,490
Why so cryptic?

150
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,630
Oh... Did something happen with Aiko?

151
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,980
No, not really.

152
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,490
For real?! I'm so curious!

153
00:12:46,490 --> 00:12:48,160
What is it?

154
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:51,290
- It's nothing.
- Right.

155
00:12:58,350 --> 00:13:01,140
Reo's hasn't come yet?

156
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:02,810
He's not coming today.

157
00:13:02,810 --> 00:13:05,750
What? You don't have a date today?

158
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,950
I wonder where he went.

159
00:13:10,950 --> 00:13:14,420
Maybe he is upset that I left without us doing anything.

160
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:16,160
I'm sure that's not true.

161
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:19,080
- Does he hate you now?!
- Where'd you come from?

162
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:21,240
If thing's aren't working out with you, maybe I could...

163
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,760
Chill out!

164
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,150
If you leave him hanging forever, he's gonna cheat on you—

165
00:13:25,150 --> 00:13:26,890
<i>- He would never!
- He would never!</i>

166
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:29,750
Gross. We agree on something.

167
00:13:30,690 --> 00:13:34,660
Reo would never do something as dirty as cheating...

168
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,000
Never!

169
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,460
You're so naïve. Reo's a guy, after all.

170
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,280
Men are unfaithful creatures.

171
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,950
You could call it their natural hardwiring, I suppose.

172
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:50,180
If you look back to the Jomon period and the Stone Age...

173
00:13:50,180 --> 00:13:54,010
they had to in order to further the development of humanity!

174
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:03,150
Did you bring that up so I could hear it?

175
00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:18,220
<i>[Maid Cafe | Spica]</i>

176
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:25,570
<i>[Where are you? Call me]</i>

177
00:14:27,690 --> 00:14:31,090
Are you worried about what Ritsuki said?

178
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:37,370
I don't think Reo's that kind of guy.

179
00:14:37,370 --> 00:14:39,460
I know that!

180
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:42,190
But...

181
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:45,730
You are worried, huh?

182
00:14:48,990 --> 00:14:52,340
I knew as soon as I saw you.

183
00:15:00,570 --> 00:15:03,670
- What are you—
- Just one minute.

184
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:05,740
Just one minute will do.

185
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:11,980
Not even one minute!

186
00:15:15,510 --> 00:15:17,090
I made it.

187
00:15:17,090 --> 00:15:18,760
Reo!

188
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:21,420
Not even a minute.

189
00:15:26,270 --> 00:15:27,780
You came.

190
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,770
I'm sorry.

191
00:15:29,770 --> 00:15:31,740
My phone died.

192
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,770
- Heal me.
- Huh?

193
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:46,330
I wanted to see you.

194
00:15:49,650 --> 00:15:52,250
What's wrong, Reo?

195
00:15:56,770 --> 00:15:58,480
Reo?

196
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,800
<i>[Kafuu High]</i>

197
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,790
Something is off.

198
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:36,760
Reo, let's play!

199
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:39,690
Sorry, I have to pass today.

200
00:16:39,690 --> 00:16:41,060
Yes?

201
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:46,590
He doesn't read my messages, he rushes home.

202
00:16:46,590 --> 00:16:49,140
Something is off.

203
00:16:49,150 --> 00:16:51,650
Definitely.

204
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:54,850
Even if I asked him where he went, he wouldn't tell me.

205
00:16:54,850 --> 00:17:00,310
But he's up to something. I know it.

206
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:02,690
How can you say it so confidently?

207
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:05,250
My wild intuition!

208
00:17:05,250 --> 00:17:08,260
Don't you mean "female intuition"?

209
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,980
Reo?

210
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:14,510
It's lunch time.

211
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,080
Please wake up.

212
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:38,590
All right, practice is over for the day. Nice work!

213
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,800
Hey, Reo. What's wrong?

214
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:45,790
Sorry. I have to rush.

215
00:17:53,070 --> 00:17:55,960
It's totally weird.

216
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:59,080
He's not talking to me. He went somewhere again today.

217
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:03,510
- He couldn't concentrate at practice, either.
- Why don't you ask him?

218
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:08,090
If you're worried, shouldn't you try following him?

219
00:18:08,090 --> 00:18:09,830
Like tailing him?

220
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:12,990
No, I couldn't do that.

221
00:18:12,990 --> 00:18:14,910
Definitely not.

222
00:18:14,910 --> 00:18:18,150
Yeah, I guess that's wrong.

223
00:18:18,150 --> 00:18:20,740
I guess so.

224
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:36,930
He went this way, right?

225
00:18:36,930 --> 00:18:38,900
But why did you come, Ikumi?

226
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,920
You two would be lost on your own!

227
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:43,320
He'll hear us!

228
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:48,810
<i>[Egawatei]</i>

229
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:54,280
Huh? But this is...

230
00:18:56,310 --> 00:18:58,710
Thank you for coming!

231
00:18:58,710 --> 00:19:04,190
A part-time job? We were worried for nothing.

232
00:19:04,190 --> 00:19:07,300
He could have told me he had a job!

233
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:10,780
But why did he hide it?

234
00:19:12,910 --> 00:19:14,840
- Do you think he...?
- Huh?

235
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:21,190
You're not an idiot, are you, Mai?

236
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:26,980
Such a great guy is going to waste on you!

237
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:34,560
What's her deal?

238
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,500
Whoa! Aiko as a girl!

239
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:42,130
Oh, Ranji! Hey, why is Reo working at your job?

240
00:19:42,130 --> 00:19:47,060
Well... I can't tell you.

241
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:50,380
Listen to the northern wind or something.

242
00:19:57,930 --> 00:19:59,980
Listen...

243
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:02,810
I'm just guessing here, but...

244
00:20:02,810 --> 00:20:05,620
your birthday is coming up, right?

245
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:07,550
So maybe…

246
00:20:08,130 --> 00:20:11,300
Thank you for coming!

247
00:20:14,870 --> 00:20:17,950
I just heard your heart squeezing.

248
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:20,420
You could hear that?

249
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:33,980
<i>[Do you have time the day after tomorrow?]</i>

250
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:39,430
<i>[I do after practice]</i>

251
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:48,950
<i>[Can I come over to your house?]</i>

252
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:50,750
For real?

253
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:54,630
<i>[Yeah]</i>

254
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,730
So? How is it going?

255
00:21:06,730 --> 00:21:09,470
Think you're going to earn enough?

256
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:12,310
Yeah... One way or another.

257
00:21:14,370 --> 00:21:18,090
<i>Oh, to be young! Youth is the best, right?</i>

258
00:21:18,090 --> 00:21:19,990
<i>Ritsuki, you reek of booze!</i>

259
00:21:19,990 --> 00:21:22,420
<i>Let me tell you something...</i>

260
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:25,170
<i>Aiko's birthday is coming up soon, right?</i>

261
00:21:25,170 --> 00:21:29,980
<i>Surprisingly, she likes brands like BBRS.</i>

262
00:21:29,980 --> 00:21:32,200
♫ <i>The secret that belongs to only us. 1on1</i> ♫

263
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,280
You'll be fine!

264
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:36,590
I'm a tight-lipped guy.

265
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:40,600
I would never betray a promise between men!

266
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:42,600
- That is a relief.
- Yeah.

267
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:45,050
I'm not gonna tell anyone else!

268
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:51,920
Listen to this! Reo has been working like crazy for Aiko.

269
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:55,690
What a great guy. Makes you want to cry, huh?

270
00:21:55,690 --> 00:21:58,770
But this is a secret! A secret! You can not tell anyone!

271
00:21:58,770 --> 00:22:00,980
You just told me, though.

272
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,750
You know...

273
00:22:03,750 --> 00:22:08,390
I think I might get a surprise present for my girlfriend, too!

274
00:22:08,390 --> 00:22:10,820
It'd be impossible for you to keep it a surprise.

275
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:15,450
♫ <i>I don’t seem to be me</i> ♫

276
00:22:17,430 --> 00:22:18,830
All right!

277
00:22:18,830 --> 00:22:22,550
There is no way he wanted us to go shopping because business was slow, right?

278
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:26,430
Ritsuki wanted to be alone with Hiroko.

279
00:22:26,430 --> 00:22:29,430
It's kind of fun, right? It's almost like a date.

280
00:22:29,430 --> 00:22:31,730
Then, why are you here, Kenji?

281
00:22:31,730 --> 00:22:35,660
What? Come on! Reo and Mai are on a date.

282
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:37,370
So, you and I can also go on a date...

283
00:22:37,370 --> 00:22:40,250
They are on a date?! Where?

284
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:44,300
What? Oh… I think they're meeting at the train station.

285
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,550
Ikumi?

286
00:22:48,550 --> 00:22:50,720
I can't do it.

287
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:54,380
I can't love him without hating them together!

288
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:56,260
Hey, wait, Ikumi!

289
00:22:56,260 --> 00:22:59,120
Ikumi? Hold on!

290
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:01,480
♫ <i>I'll steal you away before anyone gets the chance</i> ♫

291
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,420
♫ <i>Lips to exchange</i> ♫

292
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:14,910
Reo?

293
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:17,800
Yuka?

294
00:23:32,090 --> 00:23:33,710
<i>[Next time]
Isn't she Reo's first?</i>

295
00:23:33,710 --> 00:23:35,580
<i>I regret breaking up with you.</i>

296
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,450
<i>Was your sincerity a lie?</i>

297
00:23:37,450 --> 00:23:38,900
<i>This person is unexpectedly fragile.</i>

298
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:41,170
<i>Reo and Yuka were totally lovey-dovey.</i>

299
00:23:41,170 --> 00:23:42,630
<i>Would you like to have a one a one against me?</i>

300
00:23:42,630 --> 00:23:44,140
<i>Beat her to a pulp!</i>

301
00:23:44,140 --> 00:23:47,100
<i>An ex-girlfriend? Unforgivable.
[This drama is a work of fiction]</i>
